#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:4
msgid "System Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:6
msgid ""
"Emulation-as-a-Service uses configuration templates (stored in XML) to "
"assemble emulated hardware and data as specified by the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:9
msgid ""
"The effect is to create in-browser virtual computing :term:`environments "
"<environment>` that mimic the behavior of a physical machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:11
msgid ""
"When an EaaSI user runs an environment, the configuration file directs "
"the platform to the appropriate emulator for that system, the hardware "
"settings for that emulator, a disk image containing a bootable operating "
"system, and, if desired, additional content (e.g. software installation "
"media imaged from a CD-ROM or floppy disk) to mount in the environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:25
msgid "Node Components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:27
msgid ""
"Emulation-as-a-Service is a server software stack composed of a number of"
" modules working together to accomplish the task of emulator assembly and"
" configuration. Currently these modules must be deployed as a monolith "
"(all on one server), but the development team is making advances to "
"deploy the modules across multiple physical/virtual machines for ideal "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:29
msgid ""
"EaaSI stacks(a :term:`node`) contain additional components to allow for "
"sharing :term:`resources <resource>` and metadata across the EaaSI "
"Network, but core functionality is accomplished with the following "
"components:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:36
msgid "Client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:38
msgid ""
"An EaaS client provides an web/browser-based interface for users to "
"interact with Emulation-as-a-Service through `RESTful HTTP requests "
"<https://openslx.gitlab.io/eaas-api-docs/master/emil/index.html>`_. This "
"Handbook is primarily concerned with the \"EaaSI Client\" designed by "
"PortalMedia that allows for importing, saving, and documenting legacy "
"software and content in emulated computing environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:41
msgid ""
"There is also the \"Demo Client\" used by OpenSLX to initially design, "
"implement, and demonstrate new features for the EaaS back-end platform. "
"EaaSI users may still encounter this client at times, such as using the "
":ref:`\"Try EaaSI\"<container_setup>` Docker images. Please refer to the "
":ref:`demo_client` section of this Handbook for questions about using "
"this interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:43
msgid ""
"Further clients and services based on Environments created with the EaaSI"
" Client are under development within the full EaaSI program of work. More"
" details for using these clients and services will be released as "
"relevant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:45
msgid ""
"The EaaSI Client is built using the Vue.js framework, on a LNPP (Linux-"
"Nginx-PostgreSQL, PHP) stack, deployed via Docker:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:52
msgid "Gateway"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:54
msgid ""
"The EaaS Gateway acts as the API end-point, taking requests from the "
"Client/user and managing all emulation-related resources and permissions."
" It tracks emulation sessions, calculates necessary computing resources, "
"and locates the resources in storage (disk images, files, XML metadata) "
"necessary to fulfill user requests; then passes this information to the "
"EmuComp to run the emulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:58
msgid "Emulation Component (EmuComp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:60
msgid ""
"The Emulation Component (EmuComp) module actually allocates local CPU "
"resources to serve emulation sessions, and underlying emulator "
"applications (QEMU, SheepShaver, etc.) are located and installed here. "
"The EmuComp's hardware must be optimized to allow for potentially running"
" multiple emulation sessions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:64
msgid "Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:66
msgid ""
"The EmuComp locates and mounts resources in file storage as directed by "
"the Gateway. Files in storage include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:68
msgid ""
"Image Archive: Disk images and XML that make up :term:`Environment` "
"resources (system drives containing bootable software, and the neccesary "
"hardware/emulator configuration desired to run them). All Environment "
"resources in the Image Archive are stored in the `QCOW2 disk image format"
" <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qcow>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:70
msgid ""
"Software Archive: Disk images and files that make up :term:`Software` "
"resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:72
msgid ""
"Content Archive: Disk images and files that make up :term:`Content` "
"resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:74
msgid ""
"The EmuComp can connect to resources either in local file storage (i.e. "
"on the same server) or networked storage available to the EmuComp over "
"HTTP. Support for deploying and connecting EaaSI nodes to resources in "
"S3-type/cloud object storage is in development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:80
msgid "OAI-PMH Synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:82
msgid ""
"The EaaSI network makes use of the `Open Archives Initiative Protocol for"
" Metadata Harvesting (OAI-PMH) <https://www.openarchives.org/pmh/>`_ to "
"request, share and synchronize metadata between nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:85
msgid ""
"In addition to the node components listed above, each EaaSI installation "
"contains an OAI-PMH *harvester* and a *provider*. The harvester requests "
"metadata (in EaaSI's case, Environment records) from the data providers "
"at other nodes; the remote nodes' providers query their local records and"
" return this metadata back to the original harvester."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:92
msgid ""
"Using the provided metadata, the harvester can also then find and "
"replicate necessary files (disk images) from the other nodes on "
":ref:`request <replication>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:98
msgid "Environment Derivation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../overview/architecture.rst:100
msgid ""
"EaaS makes use of a snapshot-based file format (`qcow "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qcow>`_) to avoid redundant copying and "
"storage of full disk images when creating Environments. Any revisions or "
"changes to an environment are isolated and saved in a new qcow file that "
"is linked back to stored and identified separately from the Environment's"
" original disk image. The saved derivative environments are then "
"recreated programmatically to present the full chain of changes at the "
"point that the user requests to run or replicate the environment."
msgstr ""

